      "name": "smart-base-tools",
      "title": "smart-base Toolchain",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/smart-base-tools.md",
      "instructionLines": 157,
      "hasInstructions": true,
      "hasIOContract": false,
      "ambiguous": false,
      "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-skills"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/skill/smart-guideline-end-to-end",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Skill",
      "name": "smart-guideline-end-to-end",
      "title": "smart-guideline-end-to-end",
      "description": "The whole road from a use case to a running application on WHO SMART Guidelines, for a new guideline or a jurisdiction's adaptation, as an orchestrator of ten named stage skills, each with its own input and output contract: guideline-use-case, dak-l1-library, recommendation-extraction, l2-dependency-choice, l2-dak-authoring, l3-dependency-choice, l3-fhir-authoring, l4-application-brief, wireframe-design-review and l4-application-build. Each stage's output is the next stage's input. Human adjudication follows every stage, as QA and never as a gate: the agent goes on to the next stage while the last one is reviewed. The ORDER of the stages is a rule, though: no L3 asset before the L1 extraction and the L2 assets it derives from exist and their review has been requested. Read before starting any end-to-end authoring or adaptation, and to find which skill runs each stage. A request to adapt a WHO guideline, DAK or IG to a country or programme (\"adapt the immunization guidelines to Uganda using these schedules\") is this process, even when it reads like an IG or coding task.",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/smart-guideline-end-to-end.md",
      "instructionLines": 304,
      "inputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/smart-guideline-end-to-end/input.schema.json",
      "outputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/smart-guideline-end-to-end/output.schema.json",
      "hasInstructions": true,
      "hasIOContract": true,
      "ambiguous": false,
      "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-skills"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/skill/dak-l1-library",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Skill",
      "name": "dak-l1-library",
      "title": "dak-l1-library",
      "description": "Build a DAK's library from the L1 sources its Component 1 cites, and the L1 knowledge graph that records them. Read when starting or extending a DAK library, when a DAK's guidance changes, and before writing any L1 graph for a DAK. Covers fetching a cited WHO IRIS item, ingesting it, deciding whether it is L1 (declared > context > inferred), extracting the Component 1 graph, the L1 graph of each L1 source as a specialisation of its library entry, and the layering rule: the library is upstream of L1.",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/dak-l1-library.md",
      "instructionLines": 185,
      "inputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/dak-l1-library/input.schema.json",
      "outputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/dak-l1-library/output.schema.json",
      "hasInstructions": true,
      "hasIOContract": true,
      "ambiguous": false,
      "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-skills"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/skill/classify-and-code-content",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Skill",
      "name": "classify-and-code-content",
      "title": "classify-and-code-content",
      "description": "Classify and code L1 narrative content (recommendations, implementation practices, remarks, and proposed coverage exclusions) and L2 DAK slots (personas, business processes, guideline domains, conditions, interventions, medicines, and GRADE ratings) using the `terminology-coding` methodology and the `terminology-lookup` Tool. Covers the authoring-agent's four-rung reuse-first lookup, the `l1-extraction-reviewer` lane for reading and signing proposed L1 coverage exclusions against the printed page (owner ruling 3b, 2026-10-12), and the `terminologist` / ontologist reviewer lane for adjudicating candidate codings and local glossary candidates.",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/classify-and-code-content.md",
      "instructionLines": 159,
      "inputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/classify-and-code-content/input.schema.json",
      "outputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/classify-and-code-content/output.schema.json",
      "hasInstructions": true,
      "hasIOContract": true,
      "ambiguous": false,
      "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-skills"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/skill/recommendation-scenarios",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Skill",
      "name": "recommendation-scenarios",
      "title": "recommendation-scenarios",
      "description": "Join each L1 recommendation to who acts on it and during which business process: one smart-kg L2 user-scenario candidate per recommendation, from the agent's mapping, reusing the target guide's personas and processes first, then smart-base's generic personas, and never inventing a process. Step 2 of recommendation-extraction; the `l1-recommendation-scenarios` Tool satisfies it.",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/recommendation-scenarios.md",
      "instructionLines": 44,
      "inputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/recommendation-scenarios/input.schema.json",
      "outputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/recommendation-scenarios/output.schema.json",
      "hasInstructions": true,
      "hasIOContract": true,
      "ambiguous": false,
      "inSubgraph": "http://smart.who.int/base/directory/smart-base-skills"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://smart.who.int/base/skill/l2-dependency-choice",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Skill",
      "name": "l2-dependency-choice",
      "title": "l2-dependency-choice",
      "description": "Stage 3 of smart-guideline-end-to-end: choose which existing DAKs (WHO's, or a jurisdiction's adaptation) the guideline builds on. From the L1 knowledge graph and any known candidates, one decision row per candidate DAK — reuse, adapt, extend or reject, with evidence and a reason — laid out as a decision-comparison table and put to the adjudicators as a DecisionRequest. Also defines the dependency decision row that stage 5 (l3-dependency-choice) uses at L3. Read before choosing, or recording, a DAK dependency.",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/l2-dependency-choice.md",
      "instructionLines": 72,
      "inputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/l2-dependency-choice/input.schema.json",
      "outputSchema": "http://smart.who.int/base/schema/skills/l2-dependency-choice/output.schema.json",
      "hasInstructions": true,
      "hasIOContract": true,
