      "summary": "How a WHO SMART Guidelines L2 Digital Adaptation Kit is authored by a business analyst, a terminologist and a clinical SME under a programme manager.",
      "description": "How a WHO SMART Guidelines L2 Digital Adaptation Kit is authored by a business analyst, a terminologist and a clinical SME under a programme manager. folio-assistant — authoring a WHO SMART Guidelines L2 Digital Adaptation Kit.\nSource of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other\nBPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it\nby `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG.\nThe <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill\nthat implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared\nwork plan in beans/.\nEach of the six authoring tracks is a call into l2-component-edit-review.bpmn\n(Process_L2ComponentEditReview): the agent edits the component, checks, renders and stages it, and hands it on, while a\nperson in the component's reviewing role reviews it alongside, never as a gate. The track's renderer, checker and reviewer\nare tabled in the skill l2-component-edit-review.",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
